{"qid":"Q423","names":["Republic of Korea"],"title":"Republic of Korea","endonym":{"native":"조선민주주의인민공화국","lang":"ko-kp"},"capsule":"The Democratic People's Republic of Korea was proclaimed on 9 September 1948 under Kim Il-sung, a Soviet-backed anti-Japanese partisan installed as leader of the northern occupation zone following Japan's 1945 defeat. The DPRK launched the Korean War on 25 June 1950, briefly overrunning most of the peninsula before UN intervention and Chinese entry stabilized a front near the 38th parallel; the armistice of 27 July 1953 left the country divided essentially at its pre-war line. Under the Kim dynasty — Kim Il-sung (d. 1994), Kim Jong-il (d. 2011), and Kim Jong-un — the state developed nuclear weapons (first test 2006) and a command economy based on the Juche ideology, maintaining one of the world's most militarized and isolated governments.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The DPRK's international boundary along the DMZ and the Tumen/Yalu rivers is well established; territorial claims and the exact militarized frontier zone are documented but internal administrative boundaries are opaque.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: North Korea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Korea"},{"label":"Britannica: North Korea","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/North-Korea"},{"label":"Britannica: Korean War","url":"https://www.britannica.com/event/Korean-War"}],"britannica":"place/North-Korea","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"South Korea","rulers":[{"qid":"Q41117","name":"Kim Il-sung","start":1948,"end":1972,"image":"Kim Il-sung in 1950.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.